IMPORT prelude

-- National Symbols Act 2022 (Singapore) -- which things are national or presidential symbols (ss 3 to 12), the flag's design
-- (First Schedule Part 1, Second Schedule Part 1), the national flower (First Schedule Part 7), who keeps the seals (ss 7(3),
-- 12(3)), who may amend the Schedules and make regulations (ss 13, 14(1)), the penalty ceiling for offences under regulations
-- (s 14(2)(c), (d)), the Public Prosecutor's consent (s 15), and the consequential amendments to the Evidence Act 1893 (s 17)
-- and the National Emblems (Control of Display) Act 1949 (s 19).
--
-- Edition: Act 29 of 2022, informal consolidation ("version in force from 10/10/2025"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/NSA2022.txt. The only amendment annotated in the text is "[S 671/2025 wef 10/10/2025]", placed at
-- the end of First Schedule Part 3 (the National Pledge); the text does not say what it changed. The deposit's text layer carries
-- the Pledge in English, Malay and Chinese only, although s 5(1) says it is set out "in each of the 4 official languages" -- the
-- Tamil version is presumably not in the extracted text (inference; the PDF was not inspected).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0130 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. The Act is short and nearly all of it is encoded. Not encoded: s 1 (commencement), s 2 beyond "canton",
-- the National Anthem's lyrics and music, the Pledge's words, the symbolism paragraphs of the Schedules, the Lion Head symbol's
-- depiction (an image; nothing in the text layer), s 16 (repeal of the 1959 Act) beyond noting it, s 18 (a renaming in the
-- Foreign Interference (Countermeasures) Act 2021), and ANY rule on how a person may use a symbol -- the Act leaves that wholly
-- to regulations (s 14(2)(a), (b)), and none were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `National Symbols Act 2022 -- symbols`

DECLARE Thing IS ONE OF
    `the National Flag`
    `the National Anthem`
    `the National Pledge`
    `the National Coat of Arms`
    `the public seal`
    `the Lion Head symbol`
    `the national flower`
    `the Presidential Standard`
    `the Presidential Coat of Arms`
    `the seal of the President`
    `the Merlion`
    `the flag of another state`

DECLARE Category IS ONE OF
    `a national symbol`
    `a presidential symbol`
    `not a symbol under this Act`

§§ `3 to 12 -- the symbols declared`

-- Part 2 (ss 3 to 9): the National Flag, the National Anthem, the National Pledge, the National Coat of Arms ("may also be called
-- the State Crest of Singapore", s 6(3)), the public seal, the Lion Head symbol and the national flower are each "declared to be a
-- national symbol of Singapore".
-- Part 3 (ss 10 to 12): the Presidential Standard, the Presidential Coat of Arms ("may also be called the Presidential Crest",
-- s 11(3)) and the seal of the President are each "declared to be a presidential symbol of Singapore".
-- The Merlion is not in either list (it is included here only as a thing the Act does not mention).
GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A Category
`the category of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the thing`
    WHEN `the National Flag` THEN `a national symbol`
    WHEN `the National Anthem` THEN `a national symbol`
    WHEN `the National Pledge` THEN `a national symbol`
    WHEN `the National Coat of Arms` THEN `a national symbol`
    WHEN `the public seal` THEN `a national symbol`
    WHEN `the Lion Head symbol` THEN `a national symbol`
    WHEN `the national flower` THEN `a national symbol`
    WHEN `the Presidential Standard` THEN `a presidential symbol`
    WHEN `the Presidential Coat of Arms` THEN `a presidential symbol`
    WHEN `the seal of the President` THEN `a presidential symbol`
    OTHERWISE `not a symbol under this Act`

GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a symbol under this Act` IF
    NOT (`the category of` `the thing` EQUALS `not a symbol under this Act`)

-- The section of the Act that declares each symbol (0 for a thing the Act does not declare).
GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the declaring section` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the thing`
    WHEN `the National Flag` THEN 3
    WHEN `the National Anthem` THEN 4
    WHEN `the National Pledge` THEN 5
    WHEN `the National Coat of Arms` THEN 6
    WHEN `the public seal` THEN 7
    WHEN `the Lion Head symbol` THEN 8
    WHEN `the national flower` THEN 9
    WHEN `the Presidential Standard` THEN 10
    WHEN `the Presidential Coat of Arms` THEN 11
    WHEN `the seal of the President` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 5(1): "The words of the National Pledge of Singapore are set out, in each of the 4 official languages, in Part 3 of the First
-- Schedule."
`the number of languages the Pledge is set out in` MEANS 4

§§ `7(3), 12(3) -- custody of the seals`

-- s 7(3): "The public seal of Singapore is to be kept by the President." s 12(3): "The seal of the President is to be kept by the
-- President." No other symbol is given a keeper.
GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is to be kept by the President` IF
    CONSIDER `the thing`
    WHEN `the public seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the seal of the President` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `First Schedule Part 1, Second Schedule Part 1 -- the flag's design`

-- First Schedule Part 1 para 1: "The National Flag of Singapore consists of 2 equal horizontal sections, red above white. In the
-- canton is a white crescent moon beside 5 white stars arranged in a circle. The ratio of the width to the length is 2:3."
-- s 2: "canton", in relation to a flag, "means the top left quarter of the obverse of the flag".
-- Second Schedule Part 1 para 1: the Presidential Standard "is based on the canton of the National Flag" and its ratio of width to
-- length is also 2:3.
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF red, white, blue

GIVEN `width` IS A NUMBER, `length` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has the ratio 2 to 3` IF
    `width` TIMES 3 EQUALS `length` TIMES 2

GIVEN `upper section` IS A Colour, `lower section` IS A Colour, `crescent moon in the canton` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `stars in the canton` IS A NUMBER, `width` IS A NUMBER, `length` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `matches the National Flag description` IF
        `upper section` EQUALS red
    AND `lower section` EQUALS white
    AND `crescent moon in the canton`
    AND `stars in the canton` EQUALS 5
    AND `has the ratio 2 to 3` `width` `length`

§§ `First Schedule Part 7 -- the national flower`

-- "The Vanda Miss Joaquim (Papilionanthe Miss Joaquim) is the national flower of Singapore."
DECLARE Flower IS ONE OF `Vanda Miss Joaquim`, `Papilionanthe Miss Joaquim`, `Bougainvillea`, `Frangipani`

GIVEN `the flower` IS A Flower
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the national flower` IF
    CONSIDER `the flower`
    WHEN `Vanda Miss Joaquim` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Papilionanthe Miss Joaquim` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `1, 13, 14(1) -- who decides`

-- s 13: "The President may, by Proclamation in the Gazette, amend any of the Schedules in relation to any aspect or description of
-- a national symbol or presidential symbol."
-- s 14(1): "The President may make regulations for the purposes of this Act."
-- (By contrast s 1: commencement is "on a date that the Minister appoints by notification in the Gazette".)
DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF `the President`, `the Minister`

GIVEN `the actor` IS A Actor, `by Proclamation in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN, `about a symbol's aspect or description` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may amend the Schedules` IF
        `the actor` EQUALS `the President`
    AND `by Proclamation in the Gazette`
    AND `about a symbol's aspect or description`

GIVEN `the actor` IS A Actor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may make regulations under this Act` IF
    `the actor` EQUALS `the President`

§§ `14(2), 15 -- offences and prosecution`

-- s 14(2): regulations may (a) "regulate the circumstances and manner in which a national symbol or presidential symbol may be
-- used"; (b) enable a prescribed person to permit or prohibit use, with appeals; (c) "provide that the contravention of a
-- regulation is an offence"; and (d) prescribe the penalty, "which penalty must not exceed a fine of $30,000 or imprisonment for
-- a term not exceeding 6 months or both".
-- The Act itself creates NO offence: a use of a symbol is punishable only if a regulation is contravened and that regulation is
-- made an offence.
GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulation penalty is within s 14(2)(d)` IF
        `maximum fine` AT MOST 30000
    AND `maximum imprisonment in months` AT MOST 6

GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing, `the use contravenes a regulation` IS A BOOLEAN, `the regulation makes contravention an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the use can be an offence` IF
        `is a symbol under this Act` `the thing`
    AND `the use contravenes a regulation`
    AND `the regulation makes contravention an offence`

-- s 15: "A prosecution under this Act may only be instituted by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `instituted by the Public Prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Public Prosecutor consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `instituted by the Public Prosecutor` OR `the Public Prosecutor consented`

§§ `17, 19 -- the consequential amendments`

-- s 17 substitutes Evidence Act 1893 s 59(1)(f), so that the facts of which courts take judicial notice include "the public seal,
-- the seal of the President, the seals of all the courts in Singapore, ...". Only the two seals among the symbols are named there.
GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is named in Evidence Act s 59(1)(f)` IF
    CONSIDER `the thing`
    WHEN `the public seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the seal of the President` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 19 renames the National Emblems (Control of Display) Act 1949 to the Foreign National Emblems (Control of Display) Act 1949
-- and redefines its subject as a "foreign national emblem": "any flag, banner or other emblem being or purporting to be the flag,
-- banner or other emblem of any state, ...". Only the flag of another state is treated as such here; whether the 1949 Act's
-- words "any state" still reach Singapore's own flag is NOT decided by this encoding.
GIVEN `the thing` IS A Thing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a foreign national emblem` IF
    `the thing` EQUALS `the flag of another state`
